# Python
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Config / environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Generated data and artifacts — never commit transaction or KYC data
*.parquet
out/
# Exception: Model A/B are real trained, servable artifacts
# (ml/model_runtime.py), not regenerable derived data like the rest of
# ml/out/ -- the deployed service needs them, so they are committed. A
# negation cannot reach into an already-excluded parent (git docs), so
# ml/out/ itself must be re-included first, then everything in it
# EXCEPT models/ re-excluded.
!ml/out/
ml/out/*
!ml/out/models/

# Transient Vertex-registration conversion artifact (ml/vertex/register_ab.py
# regenerates this from the committed model_{a,b,c}.ubj every run) -- not a
# servable artifact itself, no committed precedent for model_a.bst/model_b.bst
# either.
ml/out/models/*.bst

# Secrets and credentials — this is a public repo
*-key.json
*_key.json
service-account*.json
credentials.json
secrets/
*.pem
*.p12
*.key

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/

# IBM AML public benchmark data (Lane D2) — third-party dataset, large,
# never committed; redownloadable from its own source.
ml/experiments/public_benchmark/

# IBM AML split.json (Lane D2) — CDLA-Sharing-1.0 publishing the Data or
# Enhanced Data triggers share-alike (s3); regenerated locally and
# deterministically by ml/experiments/ibm_aml/make_split.py instead of
# committed. See that script's EXPECTED_SPLIT_SHA256.
ml/experiments/ibm_aml/split.json

# Official regulation PDFs — fetched from government sites, never committed.
# They are third-party Crown/Government copyright, they are large, and they
# are reproducible from the URLs listed in README.md. docai/ reads them
# locally; nothing in CI needs them.
docai/regulations_corpus/

# Operational runbook — resource ids and destructive gcloud commands.
# Kept on disk, deliberately untracked: a submission repo is the wrong
# place for a list of things to delete and the ids to delete them by.
docs/post_judging_cleanup.md

# Confidential Space enclave working files.
# Digests and evidence are run artefacts, and a plaintext bundle from
# enclave_send_edges.py --dry-run must never be committed: it is exactly the
# cross-bank data the enclave exists to keep out of shared storage.
.enclave-digest-*
.enclave-evidence/
.enclave-bundle-*
.enclave-*.log
.deploy.log

# Bank-side outbox decrypt keys (enclave/outbox_crypto.py). Real private keys,
# generated offline by infra/enclave_outbox_keygen.py -- never commit these.
.enclave-outbox-key-*.bin

# Per-bank flagged account ids (hashed) that drive which accounts
# enclave/workload.py's ring-finding clusters on for a given run. Not
# raw PII, but still local operational data -- same "never commit" rule
# as the rest of this project's enclave working files.
.enclave-flagged-*.csv

# Scratch VM-name strings left over from ad hoc diagnostics.
.enclave-diag*-vmname
.claude/worktrees/
.claude/agents/
ml/experiments/public_benchmark/
mintty.*.png
